			"type": "text",
			"text": "Bajadasaurus is a sauropod from Early Cretaceous Patagonia. The genus name consists of 'bajada' the locality it was found in -alongside meaning downhill- and 'saurus' meaning lizard. It was about 10 meters long and around 4 tonnes with forward facing neural spines on its neck. The latest research suggests that these spines were covered with ligaments and were probably used for sexual displays."
